  origins: `**Mentoring research** began with Kathy Kram's interviews of manager pairs (1983, the "most highly cited" study, quoted for a mentor's parental pride) and *Mentoring at Work* (1985). Later work: developmental networks (Higgins & Kram, 2001), sponsorship (Hewlett, 2013), and youth mentoring (Rhodes; DuBois et al. meta-analyses).

**Expertise.** Ericsson, Krampe & Tesch-Römer (1993); Ericsson & Pool, *Peak* (2016); Duckworth's own collaboration with Ericsson on spelling bee practice (2011).

**Expectancy effects.** Merton (1948); Rosenthal & Jacobson (1968); Eden's military Pygmalion studies; Jussim & Harber's (2005) review.

**Network sociology.** Granovetter (1973); Burt's structural holes (1992); Lin's social resources theory; Kundu's ethnographic work on student agency.

**Gratitude.** Emmons & McCullough (2003); Seligman et al. (2005); Kumar & Epley (2018).`,
